sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor MA as Musician A
    actor MB as Musician B
    participant UI as WebClient
    participant API as SignupController
    participant SS as SignupService
    participant EVR as EventRepository
    participant SR as SignupRepository
    participant NS as NotificationService
    participant DB as Database

    Note over MA,DB: Scenario 11 - Concurrent Event signups at capacity (UC-MUS-001 extension 2b, EARS-IF-002, EARS-NF-002)
    Note over MA,DB: Given Event 1 exists with capacity 5 and 4 Signups already exist

    activate UI
    activate API
    activate SS
    activate EVR
    activate SR
    activate DB

    Note over MA,DB: When 2 Musicians simultaneously attempt to sign up for Event 1
    par Musician A submits
        activate MA
        MA->>UI: clickSignUp(eventId=1, info=Available)
        UI->>API: POST /api/events/1/signups (info=Available)
        API->>SS: createSignup(musicianId=A, eventId=1, info=Available)
        SS->>EVR: findById(1)
        EVR-->>SS: Event(id=1, band_id=3, capacity=5, date)
        SS->>SR: insertIfBelowLimit(1, A, Available, 5)
        SR->>DB: INSERT INTO Signup SELECT ... WHERE count(event_id=1) is below 5 (SERIALIZABLE)
        DB-->>SR: 1 row inserted (count 4 to 5)
        SR-->>SS: Signup(id=21)
        SS->>NS: notifyBand(signupId=21, bandId=3)
        activate NS
        NS-->>SS: Notified (email and site channels as in scenario 3)
        deactivate NS
        SS-->>API: SignupCreated(signupId=21)
        API-->>UI: 201 Created
        UI-->>MA: showConfirmation()
        deactivate MA
    and Musician B submits at the same time
        activate MB
        MB->>UI: clickSignUp(eventId=1, info=Available)
        UI->>API: POST /api/events/1/signups (info=Available)
        API->>SS: createSignup(musicianId=B, eventId=1, info=Available)
        SS->>EVR: findById(1)
        EVR-->>SS: Event(id=1, band_id=3, capacity=5, date)
        loop up to 3 attempts while SerializationFailure
            SS->>SR: insertIfBelowLimit(1, B, Available, 5)
            SR->>DB: INSERT INTO Signup SELECT ... WHERE count(event_id=1) is below 5 (SERIALIZABLE)
            alt attempt 1 - conflicts with uncommitted transaction of Musician A
                DB-->>SR: SerializationFailure (SQLSTATE 40001)
                SR-->>SS: RetryableConflict
            else attempt 2 - Musician A is committed, capacity reached
                DB-->>SR: 0 rows inserted (count is already 5)
                SR-->>SS: LimitReached
            end
        end
        SS-->>API: SignupRejected(EVENT_FULL)
        API-->>UI: 409 Conflict (Event full)
        UI-->>MB: showError(Event full)
        deactivate MB
    end
    Note over MA,MB: Then exactly one signup succeeds and the other is rejected with Event full

    deactivate DB
    deactivate SR
    deactivate EVR
    deactivate SS
    deactivate API
    deactivate UI
